ack of crew cooperation and stress resilience are serious concerns. So we should probably shift to A.\n\nThus we will change vote to Candidate A, explaining that while C's technical competence is strong, the missing evidence on crew cooperation and stress resilience are critical gaps, and A already demonstrates crew cooperation and reliability, making him a safer choice despite communication issues that can be mitigated.\n\nProvide explicit facts: C anticipates dangerous situations, sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision, leadership; but show-off, not open to new ideas, not good at criticism, no crew cooperation, no stress resilience. A: 100% reliable, creates positive atmosphere with crew, makes correct decisions quickly, understands complicated technology, but difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education, no stress resilience evidence. Emphasize crew cooperation as non-negotiable.\n\nThus vote for A.\n\nNow produce final output."}
